.TH TODO-SQLITE-CLI 1 "2026-08-27" "todo-sqlite-cli 2.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
todo-sqlite-cli \- per-project TODO list CLI backed by SQLite
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B todo-sqlite-cli
[\fB\-\-db\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-\-json\fR]
.I COMMAND
[\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B todo-sqlite-cli
is a scriptable per-project TODO list backed by SQLite.
It is designed for coding agents (Claude Code and friends), but works equally
well as a plain CLI in shell scripts, CI jobs, and human workflows.
The tool stores tasks in a single SQLite file so state is durable, queryable,
and shareable across multiple repositories.
.PP
Every command supports
.B \-\-json
for machine-readable output and
.B \-\-db
.I PATH
to override database resolution.
On
.BR list " and " export-todo
the JSON output is wrapped:
.IR "{\(dqtasks\(dq: [...]}" .
On
.B export-completed
it is wrapped and grouped by completion date:
.IR "{\(dqcompleted\(dq: [{\(dqdate\(dq: \(dqYYYY-MM-DD\(dq, \(dqtasks\(dq: [...]}, ...]}" .
Single-task commands
.RB ( next ", " add ", " start ", " stop ", " revert ", " done ", " show ", " edit )
emit a bare task object. For streaming-friendly one-object-per-line output on the list/export commands, prefer
.BR "\-\-format ndjson" .
Output is compact-by-default to keep token usage low when an AI agent reads
it back; pass
.B \-\-verbose
or
.B \-\-pretty
on commands that support it for human-readable dumps.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
Initialize a new database. Writes a
.I .todo-sqlite-cli
marker file in the current directory unless
.B \-\-db
is given.
.TP
.B add \fITITLE\fR
Add a new task. Prints the new ID. Flags:
.B \-\-details \fITEXT\fR,
.B \-\-tag \fITAG\fR
(repeatable),
.B \-\-priority \fIP\fR
(accepts
.IR 1 \-\- 5 ,
.IR P1 \-\- P5 ,
or
.IR p1 \-\- p5 ;
default
.IR 3 ),
.B \-\-depends-on \fIID\fR
(repeatable),
.B \-\-start
(immediately move to in-progress after adding),
.B \-\-gate
(mark this task as a gate \(em a checkpoint on a condition becoming true,
described in
.BR \-\-details ,
not work to be done; see
.B GATES
below).
.TP
.B list
List tasks. Default shows active work (in-progress, partial, and pending),
ordered in-progress first, then partial, then pending; within each, by
priority. Flags:
.B \-\-status pending|partial|in-progress|done|rejected|active|all,
.B \-\-tag \fITAG\fR,
.B \-\-limit \fIN\fR,
.B \-\-format table|json|ndjson|markdown
(json wraps in
.IR "{\(dqtasks\(dq: [...]}" ;
ndjson emits one task object per line for streaming/jq pipelines;
table/markdown prefix
.B [GATE]
before the title of a gate task),
.B \-\-since \fIDATE\fR
(YYYY-MM-DD or RFC3339; filters by
.IR created_at ),
.B \-\-ids-only
(print only IDs, one per line in text mode or as a JSON array under
.BR \-\-json ),
.B \-\-verbose
(use heading-per-field markdown),
.B \-\-kind gate|task|all
(default
.IR all ;
.B gate
gives a readiness dashboard of every open checkpoint and what it's blocking).
.TP
.B next
Print the single task to work on next. Returns the oldest in-progress task,
then the oldest unblocked partial task, then the highest-priority unblocked
pending task.
Skips tasks with unmet dependencies and always excludes gates \(em a gate is
never "the task to work on next". If every remaining unblocked task is a
gate, prints nothing actionable (a stderr hint points at
.BR "list \-\-kind gate" )
rather than surfacing one.
.TP
.B start \fIID\fR
Move a task to in-progress. If another task is already in-progress, it is
auto-paused to
.B partial
(its
.I started_at
is preserved).
Pass
.B \-\-force
to keep multiple tasks in-progress and to ignore unmet dependencies.
.TP
.B stop \fIID\fR
Move an in-progress task to
.BR partial .
Preserves
.IR started_at .
.TP
.B revert \fIID\fR
Move a task back to pending and clear
.IR started_at .
Useful to discard a start that turned out to be wrong.
.TP
.B done \fIID\fR " [" \-\-rejected ]
Mark a task done. Idempotent \(em calling it on a task already in the
target status does not rewrite
.I completed_at
and exits 0. With
.BR \-\-rejected ,
close the task as
.I rejected
(declined / won't-do) instead of
.IR done :
this records
.I completed_at
but does not unblock tasks that depend on it.
.TP
.B show \fIID\fR
Print task details.
By default, fields holding their default values
.RB ( "Status: pending" ,
.BR "Priority: P3" )
are omitted to keep output terse.
Pass
.B \-\-verbose
to print every field including
.IR created_at .
.B \-\-format text|json|ndjson|markdown
selects the output format
.RI ( text
is the default).
.TP
.B edit \fIID\fR
Edit an existing task. Flags:
.B \-\-title \fITEXT\fR,
.B \-\-details \fITEXT\fR
(replace),
.B \-\-append-details \fITEXT\fR
(append to existing details with a newline separator; mutually exclusive
with
.BR \-\-details
and
.BR \-\-clear-details ),
.B \-\-clear-details,
.B \-\-priority \fIP\fR,
.B \-\-add-tag \fITAG\fR
(repeatable),
.B \-\-rm-tag \fITAG\fR
(repeatable),
.B \-\-add-dep \fIID\fR
(repeatable; rejects cycles),
.B \-\-rm-dep \fIID\fR
(repeatable),
.B \-\-gate
(mark this task as a gate; mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-no-gate ),
.B \-\-no-gate
(demote a gate back to a regular task).
.TP
.B rm \fIID\fR
Delete a task. Cascades to associated tags and dependency edges.
.TP
.B export-completed
Export completed tasks. Default shape is
.IR "{\(dqcompleted\(dq: [{\(dqdate\(dq: \(dqYYYY-MM-DD\(dq, \(dqtasks\(dq: [...]}, ...]}" ,
descending by date, compact.
Flags:
.B \-\-since \fIDATE\fR
(inclusive lower bound on
.IR completed_at ),
.B \-\-until \fIDATE\fR
(exclusive upper bound),
.B \-\-pretty
(indented JSON for human review; ignored when
.BR "\-\-format ndjson" ),
.B \-\-format json|ndjson|markdown
(ndjson emits one task object per line, flat — each task carries its own
.IR completed_at ;
markdown emits a date-grouped checklist).
.TP
.B export-todo
Export active + partial + pending tasks. Flags:
.B \-\-format json|ndjson|markdown
(json wraps in
.IR "{\(dqtasks\(dq: [...]}" ;
ndjson emits one task per line for streaming),
.B \-\-verbose
(heading-per-field markdown; default is terse).
.TP
.B cfd
Cumulative flow diagram data: per-bucket
.IR backlog / in_progress / done / rejected
counts, reconstructed purely from
.IR created_at ", " started_at ", and " completed_at
\(em no new schema, no snapshotting required. Flags:
.B \-\-since \fIDATE\fR
(inclusive lower bound; defaults to the earliest
.IR created_at ),
.B \-\-until \fIDATE\fR
(inclusive upper bound; defaults to today),
.B \-\-bucket day|week
(default
.IR day ;
the bucket list always ends exactly on
.B \-\-until
even when the step doesn't land on it),
.B \-\-format ascii|csv|json
(default
.IR ascii ;
.B json
shape is
.IR "{\(dqbuckets\(dq: [{\(dqdate\(dq: \(dq...\(dq, \(dqbacklog\(dq: N, \(dqin_progress\(dq: N, \(dqdone\(dq: N, \(dqrejected\(dq: N}, ...]}" ).
.PP
Caveat: a task that was
.BR start ed,
then
.BR revert ed
(clearing
.IR started_at ),
under-counts its historical in-progress time \(em
.B cfd
can only see the current state of
.IR started_at ,
not past work episodes that were discarded.
.TP
.B aging
List open tasks (pending, partial, in-progress), oldest
.I created_at
first, for spotting backlog items that have aged unnoticed \(em e.g. ahead
of a weekly rebase. Read-only: does not change
.I priority
or the ordering used by
.BR next / list .
Flags:
.B \-\-stale-days \fIN\fR
(flag tasks with age in whole days
.RI \(>=
.I N
as
.IR stale ),
.B \-\-tag \fITAG\fR
(repeatable; AND together).
Pair with
.B "edit \-\-priority"
to act on what it surfaces.
Gate tasks remain listed (so you can still see how long a checkpoint has
been open) but are never marked
.I stale
regardless of
.BR \-\-stale-days :
indefinite openness is the correct state for a gate, not backlog rot.
.SH STATUSES
.TP
.B pending
Default state for new tasks.
.TP
.B in-progress
Currently being worked on. Set by
.BR start .
.TP
.B partial
Started, then paused. Set automatically when
.B start
displaces another in-progress task, or explicitly by
.BR stop .
.B started_at
is preserved so the task can be resumed via
.BR start .
.TP
.B done
Completed. Set by
.BR done .
Satisfies dependency edges (unblocks dependents).
.TP
.B rejected
Closed without completing (declined / won't-do). Set by
.BR "done \-\-rejected" .
Records
.B completed_at
like
.BR done ,
but does not satisfy dependency edges, so dependents remain blocked.
.SH GATES
A
.I gate
is a task that isn't work to be done \(em it's a checkpoint on a
.I condition
becoming true (e.g. "sqc has reached maintenance-mode stability", gating a
paper-finalization task). The condition is prose in the task's
.BR details ,
judged by a human periodically re-assessing it; there is no structured
criteria field for the CLI to evaluate.
.PP
Mark a task as a gate with
.B "add \-\-gate"
at creation time, or promote/demote an existing task with
.BR "edit \-\-gate" / \-\-no-gate .
Being a gate changes how the CLI's own views treat the task:
.IP \(bu 2
.B next
never surfaces a gate \(em there's no start/stop/partial episode that makes
sense for one; someone re-assesses the condition and calls
.B done
directly.
.IP \(bu 2
.B aging
still lists gates (so you can see how long a checkpoint has been open) but
never marks one
.I stale
regardless of
.BR \-\-stale-days ;
indefinite openness is the correct state for a gate.
.IP \(bu 2
.BR list / show / export-todo
prefix
.B [GATE]
before the title in table/markdown output, and include the raw
.B is_gate
boolean on every task object under
.BR \-\-json " or " "\-\-format ndjson" .
.IP \(bu 2
.B cfd
does not change: a gate counts toward
.IR backlog / in_progress / done
like any other task.
.SH DATABASE RESOLUTION
The database path is resolved in this order, with the first match winning:
.IP 1. 4
The
.B \-\-db
.I PATH
flag.
.IP 2. 4
The
.B TODO_SQLITE_CLI_DB
environment variable.
.IP 3. 4
A walk up from the current directory looking for a
.I .todo-sqlite-cli
marker file (first line is the DB path; relative paths resolve against the
marker's directory, exactly like git finds
.IR .git ).
.IP 4. 4
Otherwise the command exits with status 1 and a hint pointing at
.BR "todo-sqlite-cli init" .
.PP
Multiple repositories can point at the same DB file by writing the same
absolute path in each repo's
.I .todo-sqlite-cli
marker.
.PP
The DB file can be checked into git like any other file \(em many projects
want the historical record of tasks and completions that gives them. Doing
so with multiple contributors (or multiple agent nodes) means concurrent
edits will occasionally collide as a binary conflict; see
.B MERGING
below for a merge driver that resolves that automatically.
.SH MERGING
Because the database is opaque SQLite, git cannot text-merge it: two
branches that both touched the file produce a binary conflict that
normally has to be resolved by hand, picking one side and losing the
other's edits.
.B todo-sqlite-cli
ships a real three-way merge engine plus a git merge driver so this
resolves automatically in the common case.
.TP
.B install-merge-driver \fR[\fB\-\-dry-run\fR]
One-time setup: adds a
.I merge=todo-sqlite-cli
line to
.I .gitattributes
for the resolved database (tracked \(em share it with collaborators) and
registers
.B merge.todo-sqlite-cli.driver
in the repo-local git config (local only \(em each collaborator runs this
once). After this,
.BR "git merge" / pull / rebase
call the driver automatically on a conflicting database file instead of
leaving a binary conflict.
.TP
.B merge \fB\-\-ours \fIPATH\fB \-\-theirs \fIPATH\fR [\fB\-\-base \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-into \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-strict\fR]
Manual/ad-hoc merge of two databases, for when you'd rather run it by hand
than rely on the git driver.
.B \-\-base
(the common ancestor) enables a real three-way merge: a task known to
.B \-\-base
is reconciled per-field, preferring whichever side changed it (or
.B \-\-ours
on a genuine same-field clash, e.g. both sides gave a task a different
title); a task new to both sides sharing an id is treated as two unrelated
tasks and the
.B \-\-theirs
copy is renumbered. Without
.BR \-\-base ,
every overlapping id is treated as an unrelated-task collision (nothing is
field-merged) \(em a safe fallback, but only use it when you don't have the
ancestor available.
.B \-\-into
defaults to overwriting
.B \-\-ours
in place.
.B \-\-strict
aborts (exit 1, nothing written) on the first genuine conflict instead of
auto-resolving and flagging it.
.PP
Tags, priority, and dependency edges union or auto-resolve without ever
being flagged. A genuine conflict \(em both sides changed the same field to
different values in a way that can't be ranked (title, or the rare
diverging
.B is_gate
flip) \(em keeps
.B \-\-ours
and tags the task
.B merge-conflict
so it surfaces via
.B "list \-\-tag merge-conflict"
for manual resolution with
.BR edit .
A task deleted on one side but modified on the other keeps the modified
version and is flagged the same way, so edits are never silently lost to a
deletion race.
.TP
.B git-merge-driver \fIBASE OURS THEIRS\fR
Implements git's
.I "merge.<driver>.driver = ... %O %A %B"
contract directly \(em not normally invoked by hand.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .todo-sqlite-cli
Marker file written by
.BR "todo-sqlite-cli init" .
First line is the path to the database (absolute, or relative to the
marker's directory).
.TP
.I todo-sqlite-cli.db
Default database filename created by
.B init
when no
.B \-\-db
flag is given.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TODO_SQLITE_CLI_DB
If set, used as the database path when no
.B \-\-db
flag is supplied. Overridden by
.B \-\-db
but takes precedence over marker-file resolution.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Initialize a database in the current repo and add the first task:
.RS
.nf
todo-sqlite-cli init
todo-sqlite-cli add "fix login redirect" --tag auth --priority P2
.fi
.RE
.PP
Ask for the next task to work on:
.RS
.nf
todo-sqlite-cli next
.fi
.RE
.PP
Switch to a different task; the previous in-progress task is auto-paused:
.RS
.nf
todo-sqlite-cli start 5
.fi
.RE
.PP
Cheap re-poll for changes between agent turns:
.RS
.nf
todo-sqlite-cli list --ids-only
todo-sqlite-cli list --since 2026-05-07 --json
.fi
.RE
.PP
Stream tasks into a pipeline without unwrapping a JSON envelope:
.RS
.nf
todo-sqlite-cli list --format ndjson | jq -c 'select(.priority == 1)'
todo-sqlite-cli export-completed --format ndjson | wc -l
.fi
.RE
.PP
Export the completed log for a date range:
.RS
.nf
todo-sqlite-cli export-completed --since 2026-05-01 --until 2026-06-01
.fi
.RE
.PP
Eyeball weekly backlog trend and flag tasks aging past two weeks unnoticed:
.RS
.nf
todo-sqlite-cli cfd --bucket week
todo-sqlite-cli aging --stale-days 14
.fi
.RE
.PP
Add a gate and see it excluded from
.BR next :
.RS
.nf
todo-sqlite-cli add "sqc reaches maintenance mode" --gate \e
  --details "condition: sqc stable for 2 weeks straight"
todo-sqlite-cli next
todo-sqlite-cli list --kind gate
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT CODES
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
User error: bad input, missing database, violated invariant, task not found.
.TP
.B 2
System error: unwritable path, corrupt database, failed migration.
